          "size": "m",
          "text": "Preservation",
          "entry": "em8l8fvc",
          "col": 1,
          "row": 1,
          "w": 6
        },
        {
          "kind": "text",
          "h": 8,
          "size": "m",
          "text": "The first part of preservation was to dry it properly. I tried this in a few ways; \n-Displacing the water water with Isopropanol and letting this evaporate after bathing it a few times.\n-Kiln drying in between custom flatteners.\n-putting it in between plaster slabs.\n-Air drying in a controlled environment.\n\nThe kiln dried samples turned out the best. After being fully dry the slices were drowned in a bath of bio-resin and put under vacuum to replace all the air inside with the resin to forever protect the slice. ",
          "entry": "em8l8fvc",
          "col": 1,
          "row": 2,
          "w": 6
        }
